      "standardized_narrative": "The Syndicate's gross claims outstanding at 1 January 2023 were $670.714m. During 2023 management recorded a gross prior-year strengthening of $15.992m (c.2.39% of opening gross reserves), predominantly reflecting adverse development and adjustments to reinsurance recoveries and uncertainty related to prior catastrophe and geopolitical events (notably impacts from the Russia/Ukraine conflict and legacy catastrophe exposure). The movement is presented in the Technical Provisions note as a gross increase of $15.992m (with a larger reduction in reinsurers' share), resulting in a net adverse movement on prior years.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "Change in prior year provisions 15,992 (41,279) 57,271",
        "The Russia/Ukraine Conflict has caused significant disruption to worldwide economies, both directly through the invasion and indirectly through sanctions being imposed on Russia by the UK, EU and US.",
        "A management margin of $21.2m net of reinsurance and reinstatement premiums has been made.",
        "In arriving at the level of claims provisions a margin is applied over and above the actuarial best estimate so as to minimise the likelihood of any adverse run-off deviation.",
        "The Directors consider that the provisions for gross claims and related reinsurance recoveries are fairly stated on the basis of the information currently available to them."
